      "title": "Assistant Professor of English (26-60)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of English (26-60) - Francis Marion University Potential Students Future Pats Campus Tours and Maps Campus Map Student Life Accounting for Students Apply Now Dining Services Financial Assistance Graduate Programs Honors Housing International Programs Majors Scholarships Visit Registrar Current Students Student Resources Blackboard Campus Police Campus Technology CASA Career Center CASA Advising Tutoring Center Writing Center Testing, Counseling, & Special Services Center Dining Services Disability Services Purchase Textbooks Registrar’s Office Rogers Library Ombudsman Student Handbook Student Services and Documents Accounting Bookstore Calendar Course Catalogs Directory Financial Assistance Honors Housing Patriot Gear Patriot Marketplace Registrar Scholarships Student Employment Student Life SwampFox Alerts Alumni Alumni Gear Give Donate Homecoming Join News Alumni Magazine Community Calendar Campus Tours and Maps Evening College Facility Rental Foundation & Development Economic Development Education Foundation Freshwater Ecology Complex Gately Gallery Hewn Timber Cabins Kelley Center Performing Arts Center Regional & Community Programs Richardson Center for the Child Dooley Planetarium University Communications FOIA Requests Faculty/Staff African American Faculty & Staff Coalition Blackboard Calendar Campus Technology Career Opportunities Directory Email Facilities Management Space Reservation Faculty Handbook Grants Human Resources Employment Opportunities Policies Library Performing Arts Center Richardson Center for the Child SwampFox Alerts Patriot Portal Password Management- Reset & Recovery Portal 101 Portal Login Proxy Login Authorized User Login Career Opportunities Menu APPLY Apply to FMU Apply Now ABOUT History, Facts President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office Campus Police University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Assistant Professor of English (26-60) Home job September 23, 2026 Assistant Professor of English (26-60) Full-Time Faculty Founders Hall Posted 4 weeks ago Francis Marion University and the Department of English and Philosophy invite applications for an Assistant Professor of English specializing in Professional and Technical Communication. This is a tenure-track position with a 4/3 teaching load. Primary responsibilities will include teaching courses in UX writing and research, technical communication, multimedia writing, business writing, and first-year writing. This hire may have the opportunity to serve as the Technical and Professional Writing Program Director in future years. The successful candidate will have a research agenda in Professional and Technical Communication and experience with teaching business writing, technical communication, and first-year writing. Candidates are expected to excel in teaching and participate in a collaborative, team-oriented environment. Strong candidates will demonstrate the skills needed to coordinate the student internship program and the Technical and Professional Writing Program in the coming years. Francis Marion University (FM) provides generous travel support for faculty presenting research at scholarly and professional conferences. Summer research stipends are available on a competitive basis. Francis Marion is a state-supported regional comprehensive university with a strong emphasis on the liberal arts. FM continues to be recognized by The Chronicle of Higher Education as a “Great College to Work For.” With approximately 4,000 undergraduate students, FM offers small class sizes that encourage strong professional relationships among faculty and students. FM is in Florence, SC, a growing city with a vibrant arts culture. Florence’s thriving downtown was recently awarded the prestigious Great American Main Street Award, which recognizes communities for their excellence in comprehensive preservation-based commercial district revitalization. Florence is an hour away from the beach and within easy driving distance of several metropolitan areas including Charleston, South Carolina; the state capital of Columbia, South Carolina; and Savannah, Georgia. Requirements: A Ph.D. in Professional and Technical Communication or Rhetoric and Composition at the time of appointment (although ABDs nearing completion of their degree will be considered). Start Date: August 16, 2027 Prepare a single PDF file containing the following and send via email to englishdept@fmarion.edu Letter of interest (Referencing Position 26- ). Curriculum vitae (please include names of at least three references). One-page teaching philosophy. Copies of unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate). FMU Faculty Application. To obtain a Faculty Application please click here Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC. An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution September 23, 2026 | | APPLY Ready to start your FMU journey? Apply now CONTACT Get in touch with a friendly FMU representative. VISIT Schedule an in-person tour or View the Campus map here . DONATE Give the gift of opportunity to a Francis Marion Patriot here. IMPORTANT LINKS FMU Safe Campus Tucker Hipps Report Title IX & Discrimination Policies Clery Report Transparency Reports Student Achievement & Success Website Privacy GDPR Policy Campus Map Accreditation UNIVERSITY HONORS U.S. News & World Report Best Social Mobility U.S. News & World Report Best Regional University South U.S. News & World Report Top Public University U.S. News & World Report Top Performer Economic Diversity U.S. News & World Report Top Business & Engineering Schools TOP © 2026 Francis Marion University | 4822 E. Palmetto St., Florence, S.C. 29506 | PO Box 100547, Florence, S.C. 29502 APPLY Apply Now ABOUT President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office Campus Police University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Acad