    "https://www.fmarion.edu/job/tenure-track-faculty-molecular-genetics-genomics-26-58/": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty – Molecular Genetics / Genomics (26-58) - Francis Marion University Potential Students Future Pats Campus Tours and Maps Campus Map Student Life Accounting for Students Apply Now Dining Services Financial Assistance Graduate Programs Honors Housing International Programs Majors Scholarships Visit Registrar Current Students Student Resources Blackboard Campus Police Campus Technology CASA Career Center CASA Advising Tutoring Center Writing Center Testing, Counseling, & Special Services Center Dining Services Disability Services Purchase Textbooks Registrar’s Office Rogers Library Ombudsman Student Handbook Student Services and Documents Accounting Bookstore Calendar Course Catalogs Directory Financial Assistance Honors Housing Patriot Gear Patriot Marketplace Registrar Scholarships Student Employment Student Life SwampFox Alerts Alumni Alumni Gear Give Donate Homecoming Join News Alumni Magazine Community Calendar Campus Tours and Maps Evening College Facility Rental Foundation & Development Economic Development Education Foundation Freshwater Ecology Complex Gately Gallery Hewn Timber Cabins Kelley Center Performing Arts Center Regional & Community Programs Richardson Center for the Child Dooley Planetarium University Communications FOIA Requests Faculty/Staff African American Faculty & Staff Coalition Blackboard Calendar Campus Technology Career Opportunities Directory Email Facilities Management Space Reservation Faculty Handbook Grants Human Resources Employment Opportunities Policies Library Performing Arts Center Richardson Center for the Child SwampFox Alerts Patriot Portal Password Management- Reset & Recovery Portal 101 Portal Login Proxy Login Authorized User Login Career Opportunities Menu APPLY Apply to FMU Apply Now ABOUT History, Facts President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office Campus Police University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Tenure Track Faculty – Molecular Genetics / Genomics (26-58) Home job September 23, 2026 Tenure Track Faculty – Molecular Genetics / Genomics (26-58) Full-Time Faculty Leatherman Science Facility Posted 4 weeks ago Francis Marion University and the Department of Biology are seeking a broadly trained geneticist for a tenure-track faculty position. We welcome candidates working across model organisms and approaches. In addition to teaching introductory courses in general biology and/or environmental science, the successful candidate will also (1) provide service to the department and university in the form of, but not limited to, academic advising of students pursuing careers in biology and environmental science; and participation in faculty governance, (2) develop and maintain an active scholarly research program that engages undergraduate students in collaborative inquiry, and (3) design and teach courses in their area of expertise. Special consideration will be given to candidates who can teach one or more of the following: (plant genetics/genomics, plant reproduction/breeding, bioinformatics, and/or mycology) and who can also contribute to the maintenance of the FMU herbarium. Candidates will find an exceptional array of biologically rich resources available to support field-based research at FMU. In addition to its naturally beautiful main campus, FMU offers the Freshwater Ecology Center, a research facility located just 15 minutes from campus that encompasses 146 acres of mature hardwood forest, wetlands and a 20-acre lake. The Duck Ponds Property is an additional 8,355-acre tract of lowland forest and wetlands along the Great Pee Dee River. FMU also maintains the Wildsumaco Biological Station, a field station on the eastern slope of the Andes in Ecuador and one of the university’s International Study Centers. Complementing these field resources is the internationally recognized FMU Herbarium, which houses nearly 10,000 specimens, most of which have been entered into the SERNEC database.  The candidate will also have access to resources in a new Forestry and Environmental Science Building set to open in spring of 2027. Francis Marion University has been recognized for its excellence in education by several national ranking agencies. U.S. News & World Report has ranked FMU among its top Regional Universities in the South for more than a decade, and FMU has been named one of The Chronicle’s “Great Colleges to Work For” for the past 13 years. These distinctions reflect FMU’s commitment to excellence in undergraduate education and to creating a supportive environment in which faculty and students can thrive. As a public liberal arts university with a diverse student body, FMU seeks candidates who share this commitment and who will contribute to its mission of providing an outstanding educational experience. FMU especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance this mission and encourages applications from women and minorities. FMU Requirements: An earned doctorate in biology or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered but must have completed their degree before their contract starts. Some demonstration of teaching at the undergraduate level is preferred Expected start date: August 16, 2027 The following application materials are required : Letter of Interest (referencing position number 26-58 ). Curriculum vitae. Teaching Statement expressing teaching experience and philosophy. Research Statement describing research interests and long-term research objectives and how the work would involve undergraduate researchers. Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate). Names and contact information for at least three references. FMU Faculty Application. To obtain a Faculty Application please click here Send Application Materials to: Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University P.O. Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547. Or email to: hrassist@fmarion.edu , or FAX to: (843) 661-1202 Review of applications will begin October 30, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. About the Biology Department: The new hire will join a vibrant and collaborative department of 16 faculty members spanning a wide range of disciplines. We strive for academic excellence across our comprehensive programs through creative teaching, insightful research, and collaborative and impactful service. Faculty in the Biology and Forestry departments have established collaborations with the South Carolina Department of Natural Resources, South Carolina Forestry Commission, and other state and regional partners, creating opportunities for undergraduate research, experiential learning, and collaborative research. To learn more about Francis Marion University’s Department of Biology, please visit the department website: http://www.fmarion.edu/biology/ . Questions regarding this position may be directed to the Department Chair, Dr. Jeff Steinmetz, at jsteinmetz@fmarion.edu . About Francis Marion University: Francis Marion University (FMU) is a state-assisted regional university encompassing more than 9,100 acres and serving approximately 4,200 students in Florence, South Carolina. The university is a strong supporter of academic freedom and maintains a robust tradition of faculty governance, including an active AAUP chapter. Located in the Pee Dee region of South Carolina, FMU is within easy driving distance of Columbia, Myrtle Beach, Charleston, Charlotte, Asheville, and Savannah, providing access to a wide range of cultural, recreational, and natural resources. In addition to the Wildsumaco Biological Station in Ecuador, FMU’s International Study Centers include a center at Rhineland-Palatinate Technical University in Kaiserslautern-Landau, Germany, with a focus on the environment, economics, and politics, and a center at the University of Prince Edward Island in Charlottetown, Canada, with a focus on environmental sciences and natural resource management. These international programs provide additional opportunities for faculty and students to engage in interdisciplinary and experiential learning. About Florence and the Pee Dee Region: Florence, South Carolina, the heart of the Pee Dee region, serves more than a quarter million people in the greater metropolitan area. In recent years, Florence has experienced significant revitalization, particularly in its downtown, with FMU playing a leading role in these efforts. FMU has contributed to the growth of the city’s health sciences sector through the construction of two health sciences buildings downtown and a third building that will house a new medical campus developed in collaboration with the University of South Carolina School of Medicine, McLeod Regional Medical Center, and MUSC Health Florence Medical Center. FMU has also helped establish Florence as a regional center for arts and culture through the Steven F. Gately Art Gallery and the FMU Performing Arts Center, home to the Florence Symphony Orchestra and a venue for numerous high-profile musical and theatrical performances each year. The surrounding Pee Dee region also offers abundant opportunities for outdoor recreation and exploration, with diverse forests, wetlands, rivers, and coastal environments within easy reach of Florence. To learn more about this growing and vibrant community, please visit the Florence Chamber of Commerce’s community information page. As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in SC. An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution September 23, 2026 | | APPLY Ready to start your FMU journey? Apply now CONTACT Get in touch with a friendly FMU representative. VISIT Schedule an in-person tour or View the Campus map here . DONATE Give the gift of opportunity to a Francis Marion Patriot here. IMPORTANT LINKS FMU Safe Campus Tucker Hipps Report Title IX & Discrimination Policies Clery Report Transparency Reports Student Achievement & Success Website Privacy GDPR Policy Campus Map Accreditation UNIVERSITY HONORS U.S. News & World Report Best Social Mobility U.S. News & World Report Best Regional University South U.S. News & World Report Top Public University U.S. News & World Report Top Performer Economic Diversity U.S. News & World Report Top Business & Engineering Schools TOP © 2026 Francis Marion University | 4822 E. Palmetto St., Florence, S.C. 29506 | PO Box 100547, Florence, S.C. 29502 APPLY Apply Now ABOUT President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office Campus Police Univ