    "https://www.fmarion.edu/job/assistant-professor-forestry-26-57/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor – Forestry (26-57) - Francis Marion University Potential Students Future Pats Campus Tours and Maps Campus Map Student Life Accounting for Students Apply Now Dining Services Financial Assistance Graduate Programs Honors Housing International Programs Majors Scholarships Visit Registrar Current Students Student Resources Blackboard Campus Police Campus Technology CASA Career Center CASA Advising Tutoring Center Writing Center Testing, Counseling, & Special Services Center Dining Services Disability Services Purchase Textbooks Registrar’s Office Rogers Library Ombudsman Student Handbook Student Services and Documents Accounting Bookstore Calendar Course Catalogs Directory Financial Assistance Honors Housing Patriot Gear Patriot Marketplace Registrar Scholarships Student Employment Student Life SwampFox Alerts Alumni Alumni Gear Give Donate Homecoming Join News Alumni Magazine Community Calendar Campus Tours and Maps Evening College Facility Rental Foundation & Development Economic Development Education Foundation Freshwater Ecology Complex Gately Gallery Hewn Timber Cabins Kelley Center Performing Arts Center Regional & Community Programs Richardson Center for the Child Dooley Planetarium University Communications FOIA Requests Faculty/Staff African American Faculty & Staff Coalition Blackboard Calendar Campus Technology Career Opportunities Directory Email Facilities Management Space Reservation Faculty Handbook Grants Human Resources Employment Opportunities Policies Library Performing Arts Center Richardson Center for the Child SwampFox Alerts Patriot Portal Password Management- Reset & Recovery Portal 101 Portal Login Proxy Login Authorized User Login Career Opportunities Menu APPLY Apply to FMU Apply Now ABOUT History, Facts President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office Campus Police University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS Programs, Majors College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply, Financial Aid Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counselors Request Information ATHLETICS Sports, Events STUDENT LIFE Activities, Events Activities & Organizations Student Health Greek Life Ms. FMU Housing Assistant Professor – Forestry (26-57) Home job September 21, 2026 Assistant Professor – Forestry (26-57) Full-Time Faculty Forestry Posted 4 weeks ago Francis Marion University and the Department of Forestry invite applications for a tenure-track position for an Assistant Professor of Forestry. We seek candidates with a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and research at a comprehensive liberal arts institution. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses in at least one area of forestry, including but not limited to Forest Mensuration, Remote Sensing, Forest Management and Policy, Forest Ecology, and Dendrology. Opportunities are also available to teach additional courses aligned with the successful candidate’s area of expertise. Additional responsibilities include engaging in scholarly activities; mentoring undergraduate research projects; serving on department and university committees; providing academic advising to students; and participating in professional service activities as needed. This is a nine-month appointment. Competitive internal funding is available to support professional travel, research, and undergraduate scholarship. Francis Marion University has been recognized for its excellence in education by several national ranking agencies. US News and World Report named FMU as one of its top regional universities in the south for more than a decade. FMU was named as ‘The Chronicle’s Great Colleges to Work For’ the past 13 years in a row. As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission and encourages applications by women and minorities. FMU Requirements: An earned doctorate in forestry or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered but must have completed their degree before their contract starts. Some demonstration of teaching at the undergraduate level is preferred. Expected start date: August 16, 2027 The following application materials are required : Letter of Interest (referencing position number 26-57 ). Curriculum vitae. Teaching Statement expressing teaching experience and philosophy. Research Statement describing research interests and long-term research objectives and how the work would involve undergraduate researchers. Copies of all transcripts (official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate). Names and contact information for at least three references. FMU Faculty Application. To obtain a Faculty Application please click here Send Application Materials to: Dr. Charlene Wages, Vice President for Administration and Planning, Francis Marion University P.O. Box 100547, Florence, SC 29502-0547. Or email to: hrassist@fmarion.edu , or  FAX to: (843) 661-1202 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. About the Forestry Program Francis Marion University is launching a brand-new forestry program designed to prepare the next generation of forestry professionals for the sustainable management and stewardship of forests in South Carolina and around the world. The new program is supported by several significant investments, including the addition of new faculty, a state-of-the-art building currently under construction, and the acquisition of the Duck Ponds Property, an 8,344-acre tract along the Pee Dee River. This remarkable property will serve as a living laboratory for students and faculty in forestry, environmental science, biology, and related disciplines, providing opportunities for hands-on learning, research, and field-based education. About Francis Marion University Francis Marion University (FMU) is a state-assisted regional university located on more than 800 acres in Florence, South Carolina, serving approximately 4,200 students. FMU is strongly committed to academic freedom and faculty governance, with an active chapter of the American Association of University Professors (AAUP). Located in the heart of the Pee Dee region, FMU offers convenient access to a variety of cultural, recreational, and professional opportunities. The university is within easy driving distance of Columbia, Myrtle Beach, Charleston, Charlotte, Asheville, and Savannah. In addition to its main campus, FMU supports several distinctive facilities that provide opportunities for teaching, research, and experiential learning. The Freshwater Ecology Center (FEC), located approximately 15 minutes from campus, encompasses 146 acres of mature forest and wetlands and includes a 20-acre lake. FMU also operates the Wildsumaco Biological Station, a field research station on the eastern slope of the Andes in Ecuador and one of the university’s international study centers. Together, these resources provide an exceptional environment for interdisciplinary collaboration, field-based research, and the education of students preparing to address the complex environmental and forestry challenges of the future. About Florence: About Florence, South Carolina Located in the heart of South Carolina’s Pee Dee region, Florence is a vibrant and growing community of more than 250,000 people in the greater metropolitan area. In recent years, Florence has experienced significant revitalization, particularly in its downtown district, with Francis Marion University playing a leading role in these efforts. FMU has expanded its presence in downtown Florence with the construction of two health sciences facilities and is currently developing a new medical campus through partnerships with the University of South Carolina School of Medicine, McLeod Regional Medical Center, and MUSC Health Florence Medical Center. These initiatives are helping strengthen Florence as a regional hub for healthcare education, research, and innovation. Florence is also emerging as a regional center for arts and culture, with FMU playing an important role in that growth. The Steven F. Gately Gallery showcases exhibitions by regional, national, and international artists, while the FMU Performing Arts Center serves as a premier venue for concerts, theatrical productions, and other cultural events. The center is also home to the Florence Symphony Orchestra and hosts numerous nationally recognized musical and theatrical performances throughout the year. With its growing economy, revitalized downtown, expanding healthcare and educational opportunities, and thriving arts and cultural scene, Florence offers an exceptional quality of life and an exciting environment in which to live, work, and build a career. To learn more about this growing and vibrant community, please visit: https://www.flochamber.com/about-flo/ . As Francis Marion University has continued to be recognized for its diverse student body, it especially welcomes applicants who can affirm and enhance its mission. Applicants honorably discharged from a branch of the United States Armed Forces, who meet the minimum training and experience requirements, are given employment preference by all State agencies and higher education institutions in South Carolina. An Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Institution September 21, 2026 | | APPLY Ready to start your FMU journey? Apply now CONTACT Get in touch with a friendly FMU representative. VISIT Schedule an in-person tour or View the Campus map here . DONATE Give the gift of opportunity to a Francis Marion Patriot here. IMPORTANT LINKS FMU Safe Campus Tucker Hipps Report Title IX & Discrimination Policies Clery Report Transparency Reports Student Achievement & Success Website Privacy GDPR Policy Campus Map Accreditation UNIVERSITY HONORS U.S. News & World Report Best Social Mobility U.S. News & World Report Best Regional University South U.S. News & World Report Top Public University U.S. News & World Report Top Performer Economic Diversity U.S. News & World Report Top Business & Engineering Schools TOP © 2026 Francis Marion University | 4822 E. Palmetto St., Florence, S.C. 29506 | PO Box 100547, Florence, S.C. 29502 APPLY Apply Now ABOUT President Campus Tours and Maps Administration Policies Human Resources Facilities Management Financial Services & Budget Office Campus Police University Communications Registrar General Counsel Foundation & Development Institutional Research Staff Awards Faculty/Staff Directory FMU Organizational Chart Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Governance Student Government Association Calendar ACADEMICS College of Liberal Arts School of Business School of Health Sciences School of Education FMU’s Evening College Graduate Programs Library Honors International Programs McNair Scholars Program Provost Accreditation Continuity of Instruction Deans & Department Chairs Institutional Review Board Student Success Academic Catalog Academic Resources Research Registrar ADMISSIONS Apply Now Requirements Campus Visit Open House Financial Assistance Scholarships Net Price Calculator Accepted Students Orientation Honors Graduate Programs Dual Enrollment School Counsel